      {% when 'osteoporosis' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide">
  <h2>Bone care: separate the external oils from the oral items</h2>
  <p>The listings above are mostly external massage thailams on one side and oral kashayams, tablets, capsules and guggulu pills on the other. Decide which route suits you first, then compare within that group.</p>
  <h3>Check three things on each listing</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Route of use.</strong> An oil to be applied, or something to be taken? Not interchangeable.</li>
    <li><strong>Ingredients and directions.</strong> Two similar-sounding thailams are not the same product.</li>
    <li><strong>Pack and price.</strong> Oils come in different bottle sizes, tablets and pills in different counts.</li>
  </ul>
  <details>
    <summary>Does this collection prove a bone-density outcome?</summary>
    <p>No. Placement here does not establish one. Rely on the exact label and qualified assessment.</p>
  </details>
  <p>A fall with new pain, inability to bear weight, sudden severe spinal pain, new weakness, or loss of bladder or bowel control needs urgent care. See also <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/arthritis">arthritis</a> or <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/daily-health-supplements">daily health supplements</a>, or book an <a href="/pages/online-consultation">online consultation</a>. Read the exact label and confirm suitability with your doctor, especially alongside prescribed medicine.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'back-pain' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide">
  <h2>Back care: settle the route of use before comparing products</h2>
  <p>Two different groups sit in this grid. External-use thailams and a balm are applied to the skin. Kashayams, kashayam tablets and guggulu pills are taken by mouth. Choose the group first, then compare inside it.</p>
  <h3>What to compare on the product page</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Ingredients.</strong> Similar names can carry different herbs. Read the full list if you have allergies.</li>
    <li><strong>Directions.</strong> How much, how often, and whether the item is stated for external use only.</li>
    <li><strong>Pack size and price.</strong> Compare the exact pack sizes and prices shown on each product page.</li>
  </ul>
  <details>
    <summary>Can I use an oil and an oral item together?</summary>
    <p>Do not assume so. Read both labels and ask a qualified doctor, particularly if you take prescribed medicine.</p>
  </details>
  <p>Seek urgent assessment after a major fall, or for new leg weakness, spreading numbness, numbness around the groin or seat, loss of bladder or bowel control, fever with back pain, or pain worsening quickly. Compare <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/ayurvedic-pain-relief-oils">Ayurvedic pain relief oils</a> or the broader <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/pain-relief">pain relief</a> range. Read the exact label first.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'cramps' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide">
  <h2>Cramps: match the format to where the cramp happens</h2>
  <p>This listing mixes items applied to the body, such as a balm, massage thailams and a kizhi potli, with kashayams taken by measure. First separate external and oral formats, then compare exact directions and suitability.</p>
  <h3>Check before adding to cart</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Method of use.</strong> A potli, a balm and an oil are used differently. Read the listing rather than assuming.</li>
    <li><strong>Stated directions.</strong> Quantity, how often, and whether it is external use only.</li>
    <li><strong>Skin and medicines.</strong> Check the ingredients against your allergies and what you already take.</li>
  </ul>
  <details>
    <summary>Are all cramps the same problem?</summary>
    <p>No. A cramp after exertion and one returning at rest can have quite different causes.</p>
  </details>
  <p>Sudden severe pain, one-sided swelling, redness or warmth, weakness, loss of sensation, chest symptoms, breathing difficulty, a pregnancy concern, or repeated unexplained cramps need prompt assessment. You may also browse <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/pain-relief">pain relief</a> or <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/general-health">general health</a>, or book an <a href="/pages/online-consultation">online consultation</a>. Read the exact label and confirm the product suits you.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'anaemia' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide">
  <h2>Anaemia: read the label, not the collection name</h2>
  <p>The items here describe different purposes on their own pages: vitality tonics, multivitamin syrups and capsules, arishtams and asavas, and kashayam tablets. Their titles do not all mention haemoglobin or iron. Open each listing and read what it states.</p>
  <h3>What to check on each product page</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stated ingredients.</strong> Do not assume a tonic or syrup supplies iron. The label is the only source.</li>
    <li><strong>Dose and form.</strong> Arishtams, syrups, capsules and tablets are measured differently.</li>
    <li><strong>What you already take.</strong> Iron tablets and other supplements can overlap. List them first.</li>
  </ul>
  <details>
    <summary>Will something here raise my haemoglobin?</summary>
    <p>This page cannot say. Low haemoglobin has several possible causes, and the right step depends on your blood test.</p>
  </details>
  <p>Chest pain, severe breathlessness, fainting, confusion, heavy bleeding or black stools need urgent medical attention. See also <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/daily-health-supplements">daily health supplements</a> or <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/general-health">general health</a>, or book an <a href="/pages/online-consultation">online consultation</a>. Confirm suitability from the exact label.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'energy' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide">
  <h2>Energy support: pick a format that fits your routine</h2>
  <p>These listings cover quite different formats: capsules, a herbal infusion, a Chyawanprash pack, a syrup tonic and a liquid arishtam. Capsules, drinks, syrups and liquid preparations fit routines differently. Check each listing for its exact timing and serving directions.</p>
  <h3>Compare these three points</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Format and timing.</strong> Check the stated directions for when and how each is taken.</li>
    <li><strong>Ingredients.</strong> Ingredient lists differ. Read the label rather than inferring composition from a product name.</li>
    <li><strong>Overlap.</strong> Compare ingredient lists so you are not repeating the same herb.</li>
  </ul>
  <details>
    <summary>Which one works faster?</summary>
    <p>This page cannot promise a result or a timeline. Tiredness has many causes, and no listing identifies yours.</p>
  </details>
  <p>Tiredness with chest pain, breathing difficulty, fainting or sudden weakness needs prompt assessment; so does fatigue that persists without a clear reason. You may also compare <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/energy-and-stamina">energy and stamina</a>, <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/daily-health-supplements">daily health supplements</a> or <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/stress">stress</a>. Ask a doctor if you are pregnant, feeding or on regular medicine.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'gastric-care' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide">
  <h2>Digestive care: start from your symptom pattern, then the format</h2>
  <p>This grid runs from syrups and capsules to kashayam liquids, kashayam tablets, arishtams and a listing described as a gastritis care kit. Note what actually troubles you, such as acidity after meals, gas and bloating, or constipation, then read which listing states that use.</p>
  <h3>Three checks before ordering</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stated use.</strong> The product page, not the collection name, tells you what an item is meant for.</li>
    <li><strong>Dose and timing.</strong> Liquids are measured in millilitres and tablets in counts.</li>
    <li><strong>Kit or single item.</strong> Check what the kit listing includes before also choosing a separate item.</li>
  </ul>
  <details>
    <summary>What should I take for acidity that keeps returning?</summary>
    <p>Symptoms that keep returning need a proper assessment. This page cannot identify the cause.</p>
  </details>
  <p>Severe pain, persistent vomiting, blood in vomit or stool, black stools, unexplained weight loss or signs of dehydration need medical care without delay. You can also browse <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/herbal-drink">herbal drink</a> or <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/general-health">general health</a>, or book an <a href="/pages/online-consultation">online consultation</a>. Read the exact label before use.</p>
</section>
